{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Braided.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneBalancedRibbon","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Shapes.ZeroMorphisms","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Preadditive.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":72,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.gaugeGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.gaugeGroup","kind":"def","line":543,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L543-L556","doc":"The **quantum gauge group** `G_q = Aut⊗(ω)` reconstructed via\nTannaka–Krein duality from the fibre functor.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:quantum-gauge-group}` (categorical version)\nRef: [lusztig1993] ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.epi_proj_comp_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.epi_proj_comp_volume","kind":"theorem","line":525,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L525-L541","doc":"**`V ⊗ V` surjects onto the unit.**\n\nThe composite of the antisymmetrisation `π : V ⊗ V ↠ Λ²V` with the volume\nisomorphism.  This is the whole point of pairing the iso with the two new\n`exteriorSquare` fields: the iso alone says `Λ²V ≅ 𝟙` for an object with no\nstated relation to `V`, and `π` alone lets `Λ²V` be any quotient.  Together\nthey are a statement about the fundamental object.\n\nIt is the categorical shadow of `exteriorSquareDim_eq_one_iff`\n(`VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo.lean`) and **not** a proof of it: getting from\nhere to `C(N,2) = 1` needs the fibre functor to be monoidal and to send\n`exteriorSquare` to `Λ²(τ V)`, neither of which is available.  See the bean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.epi_of_iso_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.epi_of_iso_unit","kind":"theorem","line":513,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L513-L523","doc":"**The volume form is epi, for free.**\n\nThe co-located sibling of `def:quantum-observable-universe` carries\n`volumeForm_epi` as a *field* — \"if two morphisms agree after precomposition\nwith `volumeForm`, they are equal\" — and `su2-emergence.lean` takes the same\nstatement as an explicit hypothesis.  Under the iso reading neither is needed:\nan isomorphism is epi. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.iso_unit_hom_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.iso_unit_hom_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":494,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L494-L511","doc":"**The volume form cannot be zero.**\n\nThis is the vacuity that bean `qou-n1dj` item 3 records.  With `volumeForm` a\nbare morphism `Λ²V ⟶ 𝟙` and `Preadditive C` in scope, `volumeForm := 0`\ninhabited condition (iii) for *any* `exteriorSquare`, so the formalised axiom\nconstrained nothing whatever.\n\nUnder the iso reading it cannot: `e.inv ≫ e.hom = 𝟙` collapses to `0` the\nmoment `e.hom = 0`, so a zero volume form forces `End (𝟙_ C)` to be trivial.\n`QuantumUniverse.unitEndEquiv : R ≃+* End (𝟙_ C)` then carries that back to\n`R`, which is why `volumeForm_ne_zero_of_nontrivial` below can state it as a\ncondition on the base ring rather than on the category. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.volumeIso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.volumeIso","kind":"def","line":484,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L484-L484","doc":"**Volume constraint** (condition iii), under the **strong (iso)\nreading**: `ε : Λ²V ≅ 𝟙`.\n\n`def:quantum-observable-universe` writes \"non-degenerate epimorphism\",\nwhich admits two readings of unequal strength\n(`VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo.lean`):\n\n| reading | dimension statement | forces |\n|---|---|---|\n| epi onto `𝟙` | `C(N,2) ≠ 0` | `N ≥ 2` — admits the colour fibre `N = 3` |\n| **iso** `Λ²V ≅ 𝟙` | `C(N,2) = 1` | **`N = 2`** |\n\nThe iso is taken because it is the reading under which the axiom does the\njob the corpus proof asks of it: `det(g)` is the scalar by which `g` acts\non the **top** exterior power, so a constraint on `Λ²V` is a determinant\nconstraint exactly when `2 = N`.  Under the weak reading `ε` constrains\nthe second elementary symmetric function of the eigenvalues and the step\nto `det(g_V) = 1` does not go through.\n\nThis also removes the vacuity: the previous field was a bare morphism,\nand `QuantumUniverse` supplies `Preadditive C`, so `volumeForm := 0`\ninhabited it for *any* `exteriorSquare`.  An iso cannot be zero unless\nthe base ring is trivial — `volumeForm_ne_zero` below.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{eq:categorical-volume-constraint}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exteriorSquare_epi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exteriorSquare_epi","kind":"theorem","line":458,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L458-L458","doc":"`Λ²V` is a **quotient** of `V ⊗ V`.\n\nDeliberately no eigenvalue condition on the braiding.  In a braided\ncategory the braiding acts on the `q`-exterior square by `-q⁻¹`, not by\n`-1`, so demanding `β ≫ π = -π` would silently impose `q = 1` and rule\nout the quantum group the framework is about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exteriorSquareProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exteriorSquareProj","kind":"def","line":451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L451-L451","doc":"The antisymmetrisation `π : V ⊗ V ↠ Λ²V`.  The corpus writes this arrow\nwith a two-headed `↠` in `VolumeFromRigidity.projection` and in\n`lem:volume-from-rigidity`; the next field is that `↠`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exteriorSquare","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exteriorSquare","kind":"def","line":447,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L447-L447","doc":"The exterior square `Λ²V` as an object of `C`.\n\n**This was previously a free field**, with nothing tying it to\n`fundamentalObj` — so condition (iii) said nothing about `V` at all.  The\ntwo fields below present it as a *quotient of* `V ⊗ V`, which is the\nweakest true statement that makes it `Λ²` of something rather than an\narbitrary object.  Same defect and same repair as `adjointObj` above; see\nbean `qou-n1dj` item 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fundamentalObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fundamentalObj","kind":"def","line":438,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L438-L438","doc":"The fundamental object `V` of categorical dimension 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_vanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_vanishing","kind":"theorem","line":436,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L436-L436","doc":"**Adjoint vanishing** (condition ii): all morphisms `𝟙 → Ad(A)` in\n`C` are equal.  In an `R`-linear category this is equivalent to\n`Hom_C(𝟙, Ad(A)) = 0`, since the zero morphism is always present\nand all others must equal it.\n\nRead with the three fields above, this now says what the paper says:\nthe *reduced* adjoint has no invariants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":428,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L428-L428","doc":"`Ad(A)` is not the zero object.  Together with the two fields above this\nis what `adjointObj := 0` fails: the only morphism out of the zero\nobject is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_augmented","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_augmented","kind":"theorem","line":424,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L424-L424","doc":"**`Ad(A)` carries no trivial summand**: it lands in `ker ε`.\n\nThis is what makes condition (ii) a statement with content.  The full\n`A` always contains the unit `η : 𝟙 → A`, so `Hom(𝟙, A) = 0` is false\nfor any nontrivial `A` and cannot be what the axiom means.  The corpus\nis explicit that the trivial part is excluded: `Ad(A)` decomposes \"with\nno spin-0 summand\" (`brings-qou-axiom-map.md`) and is `≅ V₂`, the\n3-dimensional traceless part, for `SU_q(2)` (`brings-is-qou.lean`).\nThat reduced adjoint is the augmentation ideal `ker ε`, which the\nadjoint action preserves because `ε` is an algebra map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_mono","kind":"theorem","line":413,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L413-L413","doc":"The inclusion is a subobject inclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjointIncl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjointIncl","kind":"def","line":411,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L411-L411","doc":"`Ad(A)` sits inside `A`.  The adjoint action is an action of `A` on\nitself, so its carrier is part of `A` rather than an unrelated object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjointObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjointObj","kind":"def","line":408,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L408-L408","doc":"The adjoint object `Ad(A)` in `C`, carrying the adjoint action of the\nHopf algebra `A` on itself.  In a braided monoidal category it is\nconstructed from `(A, μ, Δ, S)` and the braiding; that construction is\nnot available here, so the object is provided together with the three\nfields below, which pin down enough of its relationship to `A` that a\ndegenerate choice cannot satisfy them.\n\n**This was previously a free field**, with nothing linking it to\n`frobHopf`.  That made `adjoint_vanishing` satisfiable by taking\n`adjointObj := 0` — the zero object has `Hom(𝟙, 0) = 0` trivially — so\nan instance could satisfy \"no hidden global symmetries\" by having no\nadjoint object at all.  See bean `qou-fav8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.rigidInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.rigidInst","kind":"def","line":395,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L395-L395","doc":"**Rigidity** (condition 0): every object of `C` has left and right\nduals, with `ev`/`coev` satisfying the snake identities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.mk","kind":"ctor","line":391,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L391-L391","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.toQuantumUniverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.toQuantumUniverse","kind":"def","line":391,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L391-L484","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","kind":"structure","line":371,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L371-L484","doc":"**Quantum Observable Universe** over a commutative ring `R`.\n\nA quantum universe that is **rigid** and satisfies three observability\nconditions:\n(0)   rigidity: every object has a dual.  This is the antiparticle\n      condition — a dual is a worldline read backwards, `ev` and `coev`\n      are pair annihilation and creation — and it is what lets a strand\n      bend back on itself, hence what lets a braid close into a knot.\n      It is imposed here rather than on `QuantumUniverse`.\n(i)   the Frobenius form on `A` is non-degenerate — an exact self-pairing,\n      already enforced structurally by the snake identities in\n      `FrobeniusHopfData`.\n(ii)  `Hom_C(𝟙, Ad(A))` is trivial — no non-trivial invariant adjoint\n      morphisms.\n(iii) categorical volume constraint: the fundamental object `V` of\n      categorical dimension 2 admits a non-degenerate epimorphism\n      `ε : Λ²V → 𝟙` preserved by the rigid dualities.  Formalised\n      below under the **strong (iso) reading** — see the fields.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:quantum-observable-universe}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:quantum-observable-universe","label":"def:quantum-observable-universe","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.differentialForms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.differentialForms","kind":"def","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L369-L369","doc":"`A` admits a differential calculus: the module of Kähler\ndifferentials `Ω¹(A)` exists in `C`.  Represented abstractly as a\ntype (the carrier of `Ω¹(A)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.dimQ_isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.dimQ_isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":365,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L365-L365","doc":"Every block's quantum dimension is a **unit**: each can be normalised\nagainst.  `IsUnit` for the same reason as `frobWeight_isUnit`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.dimQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.dimQ","kind":"def","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L362-L362","doc":"The quantum dimension `dim_q(λ)` of each block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobWeight_isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobWeight_isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L360-L360","doc":"Every block's Frobenius weight is a **unit**: none is invisible to the\ntrace.  `IsUnit`, not `≠ 0` — the paper says \"invertible in `R`\", and\nover a ring those differ (`2 ≠ 0` in `ℤ`, and `2` is not a unit).  The\ntwo coincide only over a field, which is why `≠ 0` survived while the\nbase ring was one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobWeight","kind":"def","line":354,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L354-L354","doc":"The Frobenius weight `∫_A p_λ` of each block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_complete","kind":"theorem","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L352-L352","doc":"**The blocks span.**  `Σ_λ p_λ = 𝟙_A`: every state resolves into the\nchannels, with nothing left over.  Together with orthogonality this is\nwhat \"Wedderburn decomposition\" means; without it the blocks could sit\ninside `A` without exhausting it.\n\nThis is the field the axiom's NAME promised and its TYPE did not\ndeliver.  It needs the finite sum that `Preadditive` supplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_orthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_orthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L344-L344","doc":"**Blocks do not mix.**  Distinct central idempotents are orthogonal, so a\nstate resolving into one channel has no component in another.  This is the\nhalf of semisimplicity that costs only a zero morphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_idem","kind":"theorem","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L340-L340","doc":"Each `p_λ` is idempotent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem","kind":"def","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L338-L338","doc":"The central idempotent `p_λ` of each block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.blocksFintype","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.blocksFintype","kind":"def","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L336-L336","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.blocks","kind":"def","line":335,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L335-L335","doc":"**Wedderburn semisimplicity** (axiom 4).  The substrate has *channels*:\n`A` decomposes into finitely many blocks that do not mix, and no block\nis degenerate.\n\nEncoded here: a `Fintype` of blocks, an idempotent endomorphism of `A`\nper block, their mutual orthogonality, their completeness, and\ninvertibility of each block's Frobenius weight and quantum dimension.\n\n**`blocks` indexes the NON-NEGLIGIBLE blocks, and vanishing elsewhere is\npermitted.**  `dimQ_isUnit` below is therefore a specification of what\n`blocks` ranges over, NOT a prohibition on the ambient category.  This\nmatters at a root of unity (and in char p), where some `dim_q(λ)` really\ndoes vanish: those λ are *negligible* — they form a tensor ideal, the\ncategorical trace kills anything factoring through them, and the standard\nconstruction quotients by that ideal (semisimplification) before reading\noff blocks.  Read as a prohibition, the field would exclude the\nroot-of-unity categories outright; read as an index specification, it\nsays the decomposition is that of the semisimplified quotient.\n\nThe corpus already relies on this shape elsewhere: `y_(1^3) ≡ 0` in\n`h3-markov-wenzl-weights` (the Temperley-Lieb quotient kills the 3-row\npartition), and `tr_M = Σ_λ y_λ χ^λ` sums over all λ with zero weights on\nsome.  That vanishing is a DIFFERENT mechanism from negligibility — a row\ncap at generic q, not a root-of-unity phenomenon — but it is the same\npattern, and it is why no sum over blocks needs re-indexing here.\n\nOrthogonality needs a zero morphism and completeness needs a finite\nsum; both come from the `Preadditive` instance field above.\n\n`frobWeight` and `dimQ` land in `R` via `unitEndEquiv`, which is\ncarried as a field rather than left to a docstring — see its comment\nfor why `R`-linearity alone does not supply it (bean `qou-w1g8`).\n\nGiven this axiom, the co-Casimir trace identity\n`tr_M(C_dimQ) = Σ_λ 1/dim_q(λ)` is a *consequence*, proved as\n`QOU.BraidKnot.frobenius_codim_universal` by linearity of the trace\nover the central idempotents.  It is deliberately NOT an axiom here:\nasserting it would assert something already proved, and would collide\nwith the unrelated `def:mass-identity` (the vortex integral). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.unitEndEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.unitEndEquiv","kind":"def","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L295-L295","doc":"**The ground ring is `End(𝟙_C)`.**  The block data below lands in `R`\nrather than in `End(𝟙_C)`, which presumes the two agree.  That is a\ngenuine extra assumption, NOT a consequence of `R`-linearity:\n`Linear R C` supplies only a ring map `R → End(𝟙_C)`, `r ↦ r • 𝟙`,\nand its being bijective needs `𝟙` simple.  Carried explicitly so the\nassumption is visible instead of hiding in a docstring.\n\nSurfaced on the paper side in `def:quantum-universe`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobenius_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobenius_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L285-L285","doc":"**Symmetric Frobenius** (axiom 3).  A closed loop has one amplitude:\nclosing a worldline on the left and closing it on the right compute the\nsame endomorphism of the unit.  Equivalently, the Frobenius form `∫_A`\nis symmetric and the Nakayama automorphism is trivial.\n\nThis is a genuine restriction, not a consequence of axiom 2: a Frobenius\nalgebra whose form is non-symmetric has `leftTrace ≠ rightTrace`, and\nthen \"the trace of a process\" — hence any mass read off a trace — would\ndepend on a drawing convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.fibreFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.fibreFunctor","kind":"def","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L275-L275","doc":"The fibre functor `τ : C → Type*` (abstracting `Vect_R` / `R-Mod`).\nThe paper asks for it to be exact, faithful, `R`-linear and monoidal;\nNONE of those four is carried by this type, which is a bare functor to\n`Type`.  Recorded rather than silently implied — the gap is real and\nseparate from the `R`-linearity of `C` now carried above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobHopf","kind":"def","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L269-L269","doc":"The Frobenius–Hopf object `A` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.balancedInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.balancedInst","kind":"def","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L267-L267","doc":"**The balancing twist** `θ_X : X ⟶ X` (axiom 1, categorical half).\n\nThis is what makes the substrate parameter `q` *derivable rather than\ncarried*.  On the defining representation the twist axiom forces\n`θ_V = q^{1/2} · id_V` (`rem:sqrt-q-ribbon-structure`), so `q` is read\noff the structure; there is deliberately **no `q` field**, since a\ndistinguished element would smuggle in as data the thing the framework\nclaims to derive.\n\nThree further things it supplies, none of which the previous\n`[BraidedCategory]` alone gave:\n\n1. **Framing.**  Without a twist a braid closure is only a *framed* link\n   invariant — `tr_M(β)` depends on the writhe of the braid word rather\n   than on the knot.  Since masses are read off knots, that dependence\n   would be fatal.\n2. **Sphericality on all of `C`.**  Axiom 3 gives left-trace =\n   right-trace on `End(A)` only, but the Markov trace closes strands of\n   `V^{⊗n}`, not of `A`.  Ribbon = braided + spherical extends it to the\n   objects the knot theory actually uses.\n3. **A legible classical boundary.**  `BalancedCategory.ofSymmetric`\n   proves every symmetric category is balanced with `θ = 𝟙`, so the\n   classical case is `θ = 𝟙`, i.e. `q = 1` — a *describable member*, not\n   an excluded one.  This is why the fix is \"add the twist\", not \"forbid\n   symmetric\": `q → 1` must stay inside the category it is a limit of.\n\nUses the in-repo `BalancedCategory` (bean `rtrb`, sorry-free) since\nMathlib has no ribbon layer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.braidedInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.braidedInst","kind":"def","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L238-L238","doc":"**Temporal braiding.**  The exchange of two adjacent systems is a\nprocess with a direction: `c_{V,W} : V ⊗ W ≅ W ⊗ V`, not required to\nbe symmetric.  The hexagon identities are part of the class, and are\nwhat make an interaction independent of the order in which its\npairwise crossings are written. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.linInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.linInst","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L232-L232","doc":"**`C` is `R`-linear.**  Every hom-set is an `R`-module and composition\nis `R`-bilinear — verbatim `def:rigid-monoidal-category`, and what\n`def:quantum-universe` means by \"an `R`-linear braided monoidal\ncategory\".\n\nThis is `CategoryTheory.Linear`, which takes `Preadditive` as a\nprerequisite; the two are a stack, not alternatives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.preInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.preInst","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L224-L224","doc":"**Hom-sets are abelian groups.**  Carried because the paper's\n`R`-linearity (below) presupposes it, and because two axiom-4 fields\nneed it: the zero morphism for block orthogonality, and a finite sum\nfor block completeness.\n\nNote this REPLACES a bare `HasZeroMorphisms` field.  `Preadditive`\nsupplies zero morphisms already, so carrying both would put two\n`HasZeroMorphisms` instances on `C` and make `p_b ≫ p_b' = 0`\nambiguous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.monInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.monInst","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L214-L214","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.catInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.catInst","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L213-L213","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.C","kind":"def","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L212-L212","doc":"The monoidal category `C`. Represented as an opaque type with\n`Category` and `MonoidalCategory` instances. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.mk","kind":"ctor","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L209-L209","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse","kind":"structure","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L194-L369","doc":"**Quantum Universe** over a commutative ring `R`.\n\nA triple `(C, A, ω)` where `C` is a `k`-linear **braided** monoidal\ncategory, `A` is a Frobenius–Hopf object in `C`, and `ω` is a fibre\nfunctor.  The deformation parameter `q` is not part of the base\ndefinition; it enters via the substrate parameter\n(Definition 1.x, `ArchimedeanSubstrateField`).\n\n**Rigidity is deliberately absent here.**  A quantum universe is\nbraided but need not have duals; duals are imposed one level up, on\n`QuantumObservableUniverse`, where they carry the antiparticles and\npermit a strand to close into a knot.  Do not add a `RigidCategory`\ninstance to this structure.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:quantum-universe}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:quantum-universe","label":"def:quantum-universe","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.rightTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.rightTrace","kind":"def","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L187-L190","doc":"**Right categorical trace** of `f : A → A`, closing the loop on the right:\n`𝟙 →[coev] A ⊗ A →[A ◁ f] A ⊗ A →[ev] 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.leftTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.leftTrace","kind":"def","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L182-L185","doc":"**Left categorical trace** of `f : A → A`, obtained by closing the loop on\nthe left: `𝟙 →[coev] A ⊗ A →[f ▷ A] A ⊗ A →[ev] 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.ev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.ev","kind":"def","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L178-L180","doc":"**Evaluation** `ev = μ ≫ ∫_A : A ⊗ A → 𝟙`.  Together with `coevaluation`\nand the two snake identities, this exhibits `A` as self-dual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_frobeniusForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_frobeniusForm","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L170-L170","doc":"**Antipode axiom 6 — `S` preserves the Frobenius form.**\n`S ≫ λ = λ`, so the pairing `⟨a, b⟩ = λ(ab)` is `S`-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L167-L167","doc":"**Antipode axiom 5 — `S` is involutive.**  `S ≫ S = 𝟙_A`.\n\nOn its own this pins nothing: `S = 𝟙_A` satisfies it, measured on\n`S₃` and `D₄` as well as on every abelian group tested\n(`computations/probes/frobenius_hopf_intermediate_axioms_probe.py`).\nIt earns its place only alongside `antipode_anti_mul`, which `𝟙_A`\nfails whenever `A` is non-commutative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_counit","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L159-L159","doc":"**Antipode axiom 4 — `S` preserves the counit.**  `S ≫ ε = ε`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_unit","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L157-L157","doc":"**Antipode axiom 3 — `S` fixes the unit.**  `η ≫ S = η`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_anti_comul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_anti_comul","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L153-L153","doc":"**Antipode axiom 2 — `S` reverses comultiplication.**\n`S ≫ Δ = Δ ≫ β ≫ (S ⊗ S)`, in elements\n`Δ(S x) = Σ S(x₂) ⊗ S(x₁)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_anti_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_anti_mul","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L147-L147","doc":"**Antipode axiom 1 — `S` reverses multiplication.**\n`μ ≫ S = (S ⊗ S) ≫ β ≫ μ`, in elements `S(ab) = S(b)S(a)`.\n\nThis is the braiding-carrying half of the antipode package and is why\nthe structure now requires `[BraidedCategory C]`: \"reverses\" is not\nstatable without a way to exchange the two tensor factors.  That is no\nnew demand on the framework — `def:frobenius-hopf-substrate` already\nsays the substrate is available at the level of a *quantum universe*,\nand `def:quantum-universe` is braided monoidal.\n\n**This axiom family REPLACED the convolution condition on 2026-09-15**\n(owner decision, beans `qou-c64q` / `qou-aawz`).  See the module\ndocstring of `QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FrobeniusHopfModelDichotomy`\nfor why: the convolution condition\n`Δ ≫ (S ▷ A) ≫ μ = ε ≫ η` — which is Mathlib's\n`HopfObj.antipode_left`, and which this structure carried from\n2026-09-14 to 2026-09-15 — has **no non-trivial model over a field**.\nIt is not merely unsatisfied by the natural candidates; it forces\n`dim A ≤ 1`.\n\nThe three theorems recording that are **not** deleted.  They are\nrestated to take the convolution condition as an explicit hypothesis\nrather than to read it off a field, which is strictly stronger: they\nnow constrain *any* morphism satisfying it, not only a structure that\ndeclares it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.comul_assoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.comul_assoc","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L120-L120","doc":"**Coassociativity.**  The \"coassociative\" of axiom 2.  Matches\n`CategoryTheory.ComonObj.comul_assoc`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.comul_counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.comul_counit","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L117-L117","doc":"**Right counit law.**  `Δ ≫ A ◁ ε = ρ_A⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.counit_comul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.counit_comul","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L115-L115","doc":"**Left counit law.**  `Δ ≫ ε ▷ A = λ_A⁻¹`.  Axiom 2 says `(Δ, ε)` make\n`A` a *coassociative counital* coalgebra object; this is half of\n\"counital\".  Matches `CategoryTheory.ComonObj.counit_comul`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mul_assoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mul_assoc","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L111-L111","doc":"**Associativity.**  `(μ ▷ A) ≫ μ = α ≫ (A ◁ μ) ≫ μ` — the \"associative\"\nof axiom 1.  Matches `CategoryTheory.MonObj.mul_assoc`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mul_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mul_one","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L108-L108","doc":"**Right unit law.**  `A ◁ η ≫ μ = ρ_A`.  The other half of \"unital\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.one_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.one_mul","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L106-L106","doc":"**Left unit law.**  `η ▷ A ≫ μ = λ_A`.  Axiom 1 of\n`def:frobenius-hopf-substrate` says `(μ, η)` make `A` an *associative\nunital* algebra object; this is half of \"unital\".\n\nField shape matches `CategoryTheory.MonObj.one_mul` exactly, so\n`toMonObj` is a field-for-field transport. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobenius_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobenius_relation","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L98-L98","doc":"**Frobenius relation**: `μ ≫ Δ = (Δ ▷ A) ≫ α ≫ (A ◁ μ)`.\nComultiplication is a bimodule map — the defining axiom of a\nFrobenius object in a monoidal category. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.pairing_snake_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.pairing_snake_right","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L92-L92","doc":"**Snake identity (right).**  The composite\n`A →[λ_⁻¹] 𝟙 ⊗ A →[coev ▷ A] (A ⊗ A) ⊗ A →[α] A ⊗ (A ⊗ A)\n →[A ◁ ev] A ⊗ 𝟙 →[ρ_] A`\nequals `id_A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.pairing_snake_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.pairing_snake_left","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L85-L85","doc":"**Snake identity (left).**  The composite\n`A →[ρ⁻¹] A ⊗ 𝟙 →[A ◁ coev] A ⊗ (A ⊗ A) →[α⁻¹] (A ⊗ A) ⊗ A\n →[ev ▷ A] 𝟙 ⊗ A →[λ_] A`\nequals `id_A`, where `ev = μ ≫ λ`.  This is one half of the exact\nself-pairing making `A` self-dual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.coevaluation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.coevaluation","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Coevaluation morphism `η̃ : 𝟙 → A ⊗ A`, the dual datum to the\nevaluation `ev = μ ≫ λ : A ⊗ A → 𝟙`.  Together with `ev`, this\nexhibits `A` as self-dual in the monoidal category `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusForm","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Frobenius form `λ : A → 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Antipode morphism `S : A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.counit","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L71-L71","doc":"Counit morphism `ε : A → 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.comul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.comul","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Comultiplication morphism `Δ : A → A ⊗ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.unit","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Unit morphism `η : 𝟙 → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mul","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Multiplication morphism `μ : A ⊗ A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.obj","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The underlying object in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData","kind":"structure","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L52-L170","doc":"**Frobenius–Hopf data** in a monoidal category.\n\nAn object `A` equipped with a Hopf algebra structure `(μ, η, Δ, ε, S)` and\na Frobenius form `λ : A → 𝟙` such that the pairing `A ⊗ A → μ → A → λ → 𝟙`\nis non-degenerate and the Frobenius relation holds.\n\nLaTeX: used in `\\label{def:quantum-universe}`, item (ii).\nRef: [kock2004] ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.instCategoryType_qOU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.instCategoryType_qOU","kind":"instance","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CategoricalFoundations.lean#L41-L50","doc":"The standard category structure on `Type w`, with morphisms as functions.\nDefined locally because `Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Types` does not exist\nat the pinned Mathlib commit (f897ebcf). ","signatureChunk":0}]}